1
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:04,980
别又来一次啊
Not again.

2
00:00:04,980 --> 00:00:06,420
我刚刚才从批斗大会过来
I just came from an intervention.

3
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,640
不不 妮可 这是员工会议
Oh, no, no, Nicole, this is a staff meeting.

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:10,200
你叫我们来的
You asked us to be here.

5
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,100
拿着 加藤
Here you go, Kato.

6
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:16,440
对 我想跟大家
Yes, I wanted to talk to you all

7
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:18,340
说一件很重要的事
about something very important.

8
00:00:18,340 --> 00:00:21,300
几百万年来哪种植物
So, what plant has been revered

9
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:22,680
因为具有愈合能力
for its healing properties

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:23,915
而备受尊崇
for millions of years?

11
00:00:23,915 --> 00:00:24,800
芦荟[音似你好]
Aloe.

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,220
你也好呀
'ello to you, too,

13
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,140
但我们专心一点
but let's stay focused.

14
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:31,089
-是辣椒 -辣椒
- Peppers. - Peppers.

15
00:00:31,098 --> 00:00:33,152
好奇怪 我们最近都神同步
Weird, we are so in synch these days.

16
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:35,200
我想做辣椒生意 各位
I want to be in the pepper business, people.

17
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:37,200
我现在就需要点子
And I need ideas now.

18
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,740
我最近几周一个产品创意都想不出来
I haven't come up with a single product idea in weeks,

19
00:00:40,740 --> 00:00:43,700
所以我在公司如履薄冰
so I'm on thin ice at NERP.

20
00:00:43,940 --> 00:00:46,240
这"薄冰"不是指我们网页上出售的
And I don't mean the low-calorie ice cubes

21
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:47,480
低卡冰块
we sell on our website.

22
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:49,246
我的继外婆
Well, my -- my step-grandmother,

23
00:00:49,590 --> 00:00:50,515
她是哥伦比亚人
she is from Colombia,

24
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:52,460
她卖的莎莎酱
and she sells a salsa

25
00:00:52,460 --> 00:00:55,300
可能就是用这些神奇的辣椒制成的
that is supposedly made with these magical peppers.

26
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,996
辣椒 我刚刚正好提起辣椒
Peppers? I was just talking about them.

27
00:00:56,996 --> 00:00:57,800
对呀
Yeah.

28
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,888
我几时能跟她见面
When can I meet her?

29
00:00:59,888 --> 00:01:03,240
把我的酱料生意卖给诺普
Sell my sauce business to NERP?

30
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,880
你应该能得到一大笔钱
I think you could get a lot for it.

31
00:01:04,880 --> 00:01:05,840
妮可想要什么
When Nicole wants something,

32
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:07,320
就会砸钱去买
she just throws money at it.

33
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:08,560
她买下隔壁邻居的房子
She bought her next-door neighbor's house

34
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:09,640
就因为她喜欢他家的邮箱
because she liked the mailbox.

35
00:01:09,640 --> 00:01:11,120
我不知道
I don't know.

36
00:01:11,120 --> 00:01:13,180
我知道 立刻脱手
I do. Dump it.

37
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,820
那玩意比一个学士学位还不值钱
That thing is worth less than a bachelor's degree.

38
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:18,480
拜托了 歌洛莉亚 我真的很需要这个
Please, Gloria. I really need this.

39
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:20,540
在那办公室里没人把我当回事
No one takes me seriously at that office.

40
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,060
我连自己的隔间都没有
I don't even have my own cubicle.

41
00:01:22,185 --> 00:01:24,395
我跟实习生们共用一张巨大的豆袋椅
I share one, giant bean bag chair with the interns.

42
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,280
我想帮你
I want to help you,

43
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,500
但 有什么感觉不对
but...something feels wrong.

44
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:31,600
你先去见个面 听听她给你开的条件
Just go to the meeting and hear what the offer is.

45
00:01:31,751 --> 00:01:33,960
好吧 我会去 我会听
Okay, fine. I will go. I will listen.

46
00:01:33,960 --> 00:01:36,200
但我不会卖掉的
But I am not selling.

47
00:01:37,720 --> 00:01:39,600
-你觉得呢 -会很难办
- What do you think? ?- It's gonna be tough.

48
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,360
她有过大量卖不出这辣酱的练习
She's got a lot of practice not selling that sauce.

49
00:01:58,307 --> 00:02:00,156
你怎么穿西装外套配T恤
Whoa, what's up with the blazer and the t-shirt?

50
00:02:00,160 --> 00:02:01,920
你是要去参加大学面试
Thought you were going to a college interview,

51
00:02:01,920 --> 00:02:03,820
不是去1988年表演单口相声吧
not doing stand up in 1988.

52
00:02:03,897 --> 00:02:06,023
我开始觉得上大学也许不适合我
I'm starting to think maybe college isn't for me.

53
00:02:06,100 --> 00:02:08,440
俱乐部里有个人说我也许可以当模特
There's this guy at the club who said I could be a model.

54
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:10,480
他说这礼拜要带我到沙漠里去
He said he's gonna take me out to the desert this week

55
00:02:10,480 --> 00:02:11,480
拍几张照片
and take some pictures.

56
00:02:11,615 --> 00:02:13,104
我劝你三思
I'd put a pin in that.

57
00:02:13,240 --> 00:02:14,460
你当然要去读大学了
Of course you're going to college.

58
00:02:14,460 --> 00:02:15,400
你在说什么呢
What are you talking about?

59
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,420
我说不好
I don't know.

60
00:02:16,446 --> 00:02:18,520
以前读书的时候我就成绩一直不好
I wasn't very good at school the first time around.

61
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:19,580
也许我就是...
Maybe I'm just --

62
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:22,080
不许你说自己是白痴
Hey! Don't you dare call yourself "an idiot".

63
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:24,000
我没要这么说
I wasn't going to.

64
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,420
我是想说 "也许我就是还没准备好"
I was gonna say, "maybe I'm not ready."

65
00:02:26,420 --> 00:02:28,320
亲爱的 你只是怯场了
Honey, it's just nerves.

66
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:29,900
改变是很吓人的 但最终
Change is scary, but in the end,

67
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:31,920
我保证 一切都是值得的
I promise, it is all worth it.

68
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:32,840
你妈妈说得对
Your mother's right.

69
00:02:32,840 --> 00:02:34,860
你拼尽全力 使出浑身解数
You dig deep, you make your best effort,

70
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:36,920
-就能找到荣誉 -没错
- that's where you find the glory. - Exactly.

71
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,500
就像那次我在赛跑中战胜她一样
Like that time I beat her in that race.

72
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:42,600
大约10年前 菲尔挑战我跟他赛跑
Maybe 10 years ago, Phil challenged me to a race.

73
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,200
真不敢相信
I don't believe it!

74
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:46,000
爸爸赢了
Daddy wins!

75
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,040
你们相信有奇迹吗
Do you believe in miracles?

76
00:02:48,102 --> 00:02:49,352
大美帝
U.S.A.!

77
00:02:49,413 --> 00:02:50,299
他当时感到很空虚
He was feeling adrift

78
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:51,520
因为孩子们都回学校去了
because the kids were back at school,

79
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:53,480
于是我让他跑赢我
so I let him beat me.

80
00:02:53,480 --> 00:02:56,340
从那以后他就说个没完
He has not shut up about it since.

81
00:02:57,537 --> 00:03:00,636
天啊 尤塞恩·博尔特又赢了
Oh, my God, Usain Bolt wins again!

82
00:03:00,636 --> 00:03:02,828
你能想象那是什么感觉吗
Can you even imagine what that feels like?

83
00:03:02,828 --> 00:03:04,040
我不用想象 亲爱的
Oh, I don't have to, sweetheart.

84
00:03:04,040 --> 00:03:05,740
我亲身经历过
I lived it.

85
00:03:05,740 --> 00:03:06,908
本来我好像输定了
All appeared lost,

86
00:03:06,908 --> 00:03:08,334
但我启动后劲发力...
but I turned on the afterburners --

87
00:03:08,334 --> 00:03:09,320
他听过这故事了 菲尔
He's heard the story, Phil.

88
00:03:09,320 --> 00:03:12,340
结果我完成了夫妻赛跑史上
And I pull off one of the greatest upsets

89
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:14,620
最伟大的反超之一
in the history of husband-and-wife competition.

90
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:18,000
好吧 我会去参加大学面试
Okay, I'll go to that college interview

91
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,200
听他们说完
and hear them out.

92
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,620
我为你感到骄傲 哥们
I'm proud of you, buddy.

93
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:23,760
我们刚才所做的
I think what you and I did right there

94
00:03:23,760 --> 00:03:24,900
应该就是传说中的"好家教"
was called "great parenting".

95
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,940
跑步故事也许是时候退出历史舞台了
Might be time to retire that story.

96
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,860
真抱歉
I am so sorry.

97
00:03:29,860 --> 00:03:30,800
我刚才太迟钝了
That was insensitive.

98
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,640
没意识到重温那场失败
I didn't realize how much it must bother you

99
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,068
会让你多么不爽
to relive that loss.

100
00:03:34,068 --> 00:03:34,795
菲尔 我只是觉得...
Phil, I am just feeling --

101
00:03:34,795 --> 00:03:36,420
不许你说自己是"废物"
Hey, don't you dare call yourself "a failure".

102
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:37,940
我让你赢的
I let you win.

103
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:39,880
什么
You what?

104
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:41,200
我其实能轻松跑赢你
Oh, I had you beat, easily.

105
00:03:41,200 --> 00:03:42,680
那次我大汗都没流一滴
I didn't even break a sweat.

106
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:43,320
事实上
As a matter of fact,

107
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,780
为了忍住不发力 我还差点拉伤了肌肉
I almost pulled a muscle holding back.

108
00:03:45,780 --> 00:03:47,980
但我看出来那对你有多重要
But, I saw how much it meant to you,

109
00:03:47,980 --> 00:03:49,400
于是我让你赢了
and I let you win.

110
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:50,620
是啊
Oh, wow, yeah.

111
00:03:50,780 --> 00:03:52,080
很合理啊 我懂的
No, that makes a lot of sense. I get it.

112
00:03:52,080 --> 00:03:53,050
就像其他马
Like the way all the other horses

113
00:03:53,050 --> 00:03:54,440
希望"秘书"好过些一样
wanted Secretariat to feel good.

114
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:55,720
现在你成"秘书"了
Now you're Secretariat?

115
00:03:55,720 --> 00:03:56,520
我不知道
I don't know.

116
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,660
"秘书"有娶了一个疯子吗
Was Secretariat married to a crazy person?

117
00:03:58,660 --> 00:04:02,160
天啊 菲尔 百分百是我让你赢的
Oh, God, Phil, I 100% let you win.

118
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:05,460
那你也百分百可以再赢我啊
Then, you could 100% beat me again.

119
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:07,340
我当然可以 同样的路线吗
Oh, I could. Same course?

120
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:08,317
我比那时更强壮了
I've only gotten stronger.

121
00:04:08,317 --> 00:04:09,900
我们再多加几个挑战怎么样
How 'bout we add a few challenges?

122
00:04:09,900 --> 00:04:11,080
攀架
Monkey bars?

123
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:12,420
太棒 爬绳
Great! Rope climb.

124
00:04:12,420 --> 00:04:13,700
我爱 轮胎
I love it. Tires.

125
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:14,980
有何不可 中午进行
Why not? Noon?

126
00:04:14,980 --> 00:04:16,580
行 我要带人看房 但我可以移期
Fine. I have a showing. I'll move it.

127
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,820
希望你的身躯也还移得动啊
Hope it's not too heavy.

128
00:04:20,724 --> 00:04:22,465
随警巡逻的授权表真是
The release form for this ride-along is --

129
00:04:22,465 --> 00:04:24,060
详尽得惊人啊
is shockingly thorough.

130
00:04:24,060 --> 00:04:25,920
我不会让你们遇到任何危险
I'm not gonna let anything happen to you.

131
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,480
我不想再埋葬一个随警巡逻员了
I can't bury another ride-along.

132
00:04:27,480 --> 00:04:30,880
我是这个辖区的笑料
I'm kind of the precinct cut up.

133
00:04:30,880 --> 00:04:32,400
好了 米奇尔 不会有事的
Okay. Mitchell, it'll be fine.

134
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:33,760
他们天天干这个
They do these things all the time.

135
00:04:33,793 --> 00:04:34,868
你倒说得轻巧
Yeah, easy for you to say.

136
00:04:34,900 --> 00:04:36,460
我的脑袋跟某黑帮专属色撞色
My entire head is a gang color.

137
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:37,680
这真是太令人兴奋了
Okay, this is so exciting.

138
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:39,340
你知道吗 我上辈子
You know, in my alternate life,

139
00:04:39,340 --> 00:04:40,529
就是个警察
I'm a -- I'm a cop.

140
00:04:40,529 --> 00:04:41,757
你上辈子不是
I-I thought that your alternate life

141
00:04:41,840 --> 00:04:43,980
教迷途少年跳街舞的吗
was you teaching at-risk youth to street dance.

142
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:46,080
不 我是教他们通过跳街舞
No, I teach them to believe in themselves

143
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:47,201
学会相信自己
through street dance.

144
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:49,190
小卡总想去随警巡逻
Cam's always wanted to go on a ride-along.

145
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,980
于是我叫我
So, I called in a favor

146
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:53,300
在地检署上班的法学院朋友露西帮忙
to my law school friend Lucy at the DA's office.

147
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,720
奇怪的是 他们部门缺人
Weird thing, they're understaffed.

148
00:04:55,720 --> 00:04:57,860
她邀我去当检察官
And she offered me a job as a prosecutor.

149
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,880
我想象不出自己戴检察官徽的样子
I just -- I can't picture myself with a badge.

150
00:05:00,880 --> 00:05:03,340
毕竟我已经痛恨我钱包有多厚了
I mean, I already hate how thick my wallet is.

151
00:05:03,340 --> 00:05:05,380
我们什么时候撇了
So, when do we roll?

152
00:05:05,548 --> 00:05:07,440
-你是指出发吗 -收到
- You mean leave? - Oh, copy that.

153
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,060
我很难忍住不说行话
You know, it's hard for me not to use the lingo.

154
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,280
我自己也算是法界先锋
Bit of a lawman myself,

155
00:05:10,280 --> 00:05:12,560
在高中担任代理副校长
acting high-school vice principal.

156
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,098
他们给我取名号"关节炎"
Anyway, they call me "arthritis"

157
00:05:14,098 --> 00:05:16,338
因为我不让高四学生[老年人]好过
because I make life hard on seniors.

158
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:17,420
没人这么叫你
They don't.

159
00:05:17,429 --> 00:05:19,655
但他自己做了名牌放到办公桌上 对吧
But he did make a sign for his desk, didn't ya?

160
00:05:20,565 --> 00:05:22,669
你不觉得你有点用力过猛了吗
Do you think that perhaps you're coming on a tad strong?

161
00:05:22,679 --> 00:05:24,490
不 我认为斯塔勃利斯基警官
No, I think Officer Stablitzky

162
00:05:24,500 --> 00:05:26,440
会很欣赏我懂行话
appreciates me knowing the language.

163
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:27,276
就像去意大利时
It's, like, when you go to Italy,

164
00:05:27,276 --> 00:05:28,368
每两个字中间插句"甭客气"[意语]
you use "prego" every other word.

165
00:05:28,368 --> 00:05:29,598
-他们特喜欢 -非法闯入现行
- They love it. - Break-in in progress.

166
00:05:29,598 --> 00:05:30,462
库伯与奥林匹克街
Cooper and Olympic.

167
00:05:30,462 --> 00:05:31,940
-等等 她说什么 -现行
- Wait. What was that? - In progress?

168
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:33,400
我们该等他们犯完案再去吗
Should we wait 'til they're done?

169
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:35,640
-12A3响应 -收到 12A3
- 12-A-3 responding. - Copy 12-A-3.

170
00:05:35,640 --> 00:05:37,840
米奇尔 不如你坐副驾驶吧
Mitchell, why don't you ride shotgun?

171
00:05:37,840 --> 00:05:39,287
不 他坐激流勇进时
Oh, no, You know, he doesn't do that well

172
00:05:39,287 --> 00:05:40,880
在前排吓坏了 所以...
on Splash Mountain in the front seat, so...

173
00:05:40,880 --> 00:05:41,835
他不会有事的 上车
He'll be fine. Get in.

174
00:05:41,835 --> 00:05:42,780
遵命 警官 好的
Yes, sir. Okay.

175
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:44,080
那好 那或许
Okay, and then, you know, then,

176
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,925
每一个案子我俩轮换坐前座
maybe I can front seat on even crimes.

177
00:05:45,925 --> 00:05:48,010
-这样才公平 -还是不要了
- You know, to keep it fair. - Probably not.

178
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:52,660
菲尔 现在退出还不迟
You know, Phil, it's not too late to back out.

179
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:54,780
我的身体状况在人生巅峰
I am in the best shape of my life.

180
00:05:54,780 --> 00:05:56,260
上次去体检后
After my last physical,

181
00:05:56,260 --> 00:05:58,600
医生把我的应激试验结果发到社交网站上了
the doctor posted my stress test on his Instagram.

182
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,217
亲爱的 我每周去篮球场锻炼四天
Honey, I'm on the basketball court four days a week.

183
00:06:00,217 --> 00:06:01,610
他们都叫我"菲尔·灌篮菲人"
They call me "Phil Dunk-phy".

184
00:06:01,610 --> 00:06:02,690
你好好看看我的脸
Well, take a good look at this face

185
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:04,329
因为你接下来只能看到我的后脑勺了
'cause it's the last time ou're gonna see it for a while --

186
00:06:04,329 --> 00:06:06,332
各就各位 预备 跑
on your mark, get set, go!

187
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:12,820
我立即拉伤了肌肉
I immediately pulled that muscle

188
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:14,100
就是从头顶
that runs from the top of your head

189
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:15,500
一直到脚底的那条
down to the bottom of your feet.

190
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:16,587
事实是
The truth is,

191
00:06:16,587 --> 00:06:19,780
我被夹在工作和不想去健身之间
between work and not wanting to workout,

192
00:06:19,780 --> 00:06:21,680
所以根本没怎么去健身
I hadn't worked out that much.

193
00:06:21,680 --> 00:06:23,318
欢迎来到丛林 克莱尔
Welcome to the jungle, Claire.

194
00:06:23,318 --> 00:06:26,230
猴哥一盯上你 猴哥...
Monkey see, monkey d-

195
00:06:26,230 --> 00:06:29,240
我的第一反应是我的双肩都中弹了
My first thought was that I had been shot in both shoulders.

196
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:31,640
是这样的 在克莱尔去健身时
Here's the thing -- while Claire works out,

197
00:06:31,640 --> 00:06:33,780
我的确去了篮球场
I do go to the basketball court,

198
00:06:33,817 --> 00:06:37,402
但是去参加机器人大战
but, uh, for epic robot battles.

199
00:06:39,957 --> 00:06:42,558
旋转争霸者又将我堵死了
Oh, Spin-a-tron cornered me again.

200
00:06:42,626 --> 00:06:44,164
看来我被你消灭了
Looks like you got me dead --

201
00:06:44,201 --> 00:06:45,529
负鼠拳
Possum-punch!

202
00:06:45,565 --> 00:06:48,317
负鼠拳 负鼠拳
Possum-punch! Possum-punch!

203
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:57,867
云朵看起来有点不妙
Clouds look kind of ominous, huh?

204
00:06:57,867 --> 00:06:59,359
好像有雨滴到我身上了
Kind of felt a raindrop.

205
00:06:59,395 --> 00:07:01,224
-或许我们该改天再... -好
- Maybe we should res- - Okay.

206
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,300
抱歉我们没赶上抢劫
Sorry we missed that robbery.

207
00:07:03,300 --> 00:07:04,801
要能那样开始一天该多带劲
It would've been a fun way to start the day.

208
00:07:04,801 --> 00:07:07,740
你们有没有考虑过用导航应用
Yeah, hi. Have you guys considered using the Waze app.

209
00:07:07,740 --> 00:07:08,969
我可以打开
I could fire it up

210
00:07:08,969 --> 00:07:10,743
然后做你们的引路鹅
and it'd be kind of, like, your Goose.

211
00:07:10,743 --> 00:07:12,180
-你看到了吗 -看到什么
- Whoa, did you see that? - See what?

212
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:13,680
我被挡住了 什么都看不见
I'm blocked. I can't see anything.

213
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:15,640
那个混蛋刚刚超了那位婆婆的车
That jerk just cut off that old lady.

214
00:07:15,707 --> 00:07:17,383
-想吓唬他一下吗 -吓唬谁
- Wanna mess with him? - Mess with who?

215
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:18,380
这样合规矩吗
Is that allowed?

216
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:20,240
他能怎么办 报警吗
What's he gonna do, call the cops?

217
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:21,359
你们能大点声说话吗
Can you speak up a little bit?

218
00:07:21,359 --> 00:07:23,080
我跟不上了
I'm losing the thread.

219
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:23,980
警笛在那
That's the siren.

220
00:07:23,980 --> 00:07:25,960
-好的 -先别开
- Okay. ?- Not yet.

221
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,540
别开
Not yet.

222
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,360
现在
Now!

223
00:07:28,360 --> 00:07:28,848
我的天
Oh, my God!

224
00:07:28,848 --> 00:07:30,522
他慌了 他靠边停了
He's freaked out. Oh, he's pulling over.

225
00:07:30,522 --> 00:07:33,180
-戴上墨镜瞪他 -好的
- Put these on and glare at him. - ?Okay, okay.

226
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:36,035
没错 你知道你犯错误了
That's right. You know you were bad.

227
00:07:36,035 --> 00:07:39,330
像狗一样坐那反省去
Sit in your shame like a dog!

228
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,423
你天生是这块料
?You're a natural.

229
00:07:41,423 --> 00:07:43,480
我的天 太爽了
Oh, my God, that was such a rush.

230
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:45,962
我猜揍人或边跑边接到球
I imagine that's what it feels like to punch a guy or --

231
00:07:45,962 --> 00:07:47,849
就是这种感觉
or catch a ball while running.

232
00:07:47,849 --> 00:07:49,326
两位话痨 注意前方
Oh, hey, Chatty-Cathys, heads up.

233
00:07:49,326 --> 00:07:51,336
-那边可能有代号10-99事项 -什么
- Possible 10-99 right over here. - What?

234
00:07:51,680 --> 00:07:53,980
那边有两个下三滥在做现金交易
Couple low lifes over there exchanging cash-money.

235
00:07:54,064 --> 00:07:55,900
-那边 -因为那是报刊亭
- Right here? ?- That's because it's a newsstand.

236
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,780
我还很确定1099是填报税表时用的
And I'm pretty sure a 1099 is a tax form.

237
00:07:58,046 --> 00:07:59,412
-小卡 -是的 如今干什么都得填表
- Oh, Cam. - Oh, yeah, well, what isn't a form these days?

238
00:07:59,678 --> 00:08:00,877
我都被校董事会的文件活埋了
School board's got me buried in paperwork.

239
00:08:01,142 --> 00:08:02,874
我去上个厕所都得三个人签字批准
I gotta get three John Hancocks just to take a leak.

240
00:08:03,140 --> 00:08:04,560
你瞧 我们是一样的
We're the same, see?

241
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,460
容我打断一下
Oh, if I can interrupt for just one second.

242
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:08,460
我一直在输入车牌号
I've been typing license plates numbers --

243
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:09,800
你说我可以
as you said I could --

244
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:12,220
这辆脏车里的这家伙
and this guy in this dirty car here,

245
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,030
正因为未付子女赡养费被缉
he has a warrant for unpaid child support.

246
00:08:14,030 --> 00:08:15,370
很敏锐 阿普里
Good catch, Pritch.

247
00:08:15,400 --> 00:08:16,647
现在他连昵称都有了
He gets a nickname now?!

248
00:08:16,647 --> 00:08:19,786
-贼头鼠脑的 -是啊
- Hmm, looking squirrely. - Yeah.

249
00:08:20,860 --> 00:08:22,980
没错 他逃跑了
Yep, we got a runner!

250
00:08:22,980 --> 00:08:23,915
跟紧我
?Stick by me.

251
00:08:23,915 --> 00:08:25,300
我的天 真要去抓人
Oh, my God, is this happening?

252
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,740
真要去抓人 好的
This is happening. Okay.

253
00:08:26,740 --> 00:08:28,264
两位 两位
Hey, guys? Guys?

254
00:08:28,264 --> 00:08:30,820
后座没有门把手 我也想去
There's no handles back here! I wanna come!

255
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:36,240
卢克 我读过你的申请论文了
Well, Luke, I read your essay.

256
00:08:36,240 --> 00:08:37,880
你很有勇气
Took a lot of guts to admit

257
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,660
承认一年前没准备好读大学
you weren't ready for college a year ago.

258
00:08:39,660 --> 00:08:42,800
当时我还很不成熟
I had a lot of growing up to do.

259
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:44,980
于是我找了工作 自己付账单
So, I got a job, I paid my bills,

260
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:46,920
我上网读华尔街日报
and I read the Wall Street Journal online

261
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,740
直到我看完了五篇免费文章的额度
until I used up my five free articles.

262
00:08:48,740 --> 00:08:51,200
从你的信用评分来看
Well, based on your credit score,

263
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,820
红杉社区大学欢迎你入读
we'd like to welcome you to Sequoia Community College.

264
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:54,851
谢谢
Thank you!

265
00:08:54,851 --> 00:08:56,323
一旦你走过十五道
And once your walk through

266
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:59,580
运输安全局认可的金属探测器
one of our 15 TSA-approved metal detectors,

267
00:08:59,580 --> 00:09:01,260
一切皆有可能
anything is possible.

268
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:02,400
课业很难吗
How hard is it?

269
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:03,820
我们的大多数学生
Well, most of our students report

270
00:09:03,820 --> 00:09:06,340
每周做十到十五小时的
about 10 to 15 hours of homework a week

271
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:07,480
课后作业
in addition to class time.

272
00:09:07,480 --> 00:09:08,760
听起来像正经大学似的
That sounds like real college.

273
00:09:08,760 --> 00:09:10,220
这就是正经大学
This is a real college.

274
00:09:10,220 --> 00:09:12,000
需要付出很多努力
And it's a lot of hard work.

275
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:13,840
但你在这里用功两年
But, you put in your two years here,

276
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:15,040
然后转学到正经...
then transfer to a real --

277
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,880
到四年制大学
to a four-year college

278
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:19,640
就能找到入门级工作
and you will land an entry-level job.

279
00:09:19,640 --> 00:09:20,620
谈不上光鲜
Nothing too glamorous,

280
00:09:20,620 --> 00:09:23,200
但你付出努力 向上爬
but you pay your dues, climb the ladder.

281
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:24,600
等你四十五岁时
By the time you're 45,

282
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:26,980
你就能住上三间卧室有栅栏的房子了
you're living in a three-bedroom house with a picket fence!

283
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:31,460
三间卧室有栅栏的房子
Three-bedroom house with a picket fence?

284
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:34,180
我家不就是吗
Already got one of those.

285
00:09:34,180 --> 00:09:36,020
在这还能免费洗衣吃饭看有线电视
Plus, free meals, laundry, and cable.

286
00:09:36,020 --> 00:09:37,800
我已经实现梦想了
I am living the dream.

287
00:09:37,800 --> 00:09:39,055
知道我怎么想吗
You know what I say?

288
00:09:39,055 --> 00:09:41,146
"谁需要读大学啊"
"Who needs college?"

289
00:09:42,595 --> 00:09:45,200
刚才做得好 我请你吃甜甜圈
Great work out there. I'm getting you a donut.

290
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:45,900
你应得的
You earned it.

291
00:09:46,190 --> 00:09:47,946
警察吃甜甜圈 不会太符合刻板印象吗
Er, a donut. Isn't that a little on the nose?

292
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:49,120
太合胃口才对吧
And a lot on the belly.

293
00:09:49,120 --> 00:09:50,001
勃利斯
Ah, Blitz!

294
00:09:50,001 --> 00:09:50,640
二位 二位
Okay, guys, guys.

295
00:09:50,640 --> 00:09:53,820
后座还是打不开门
The door handle situation really hasn't changed.

296
00:09:53,874 --> 00:09:55,602
-抱歉 -没错
- Oh, sorry. - Yeah.

297
00:09:55,760 --> 00:09:56,620
我给他开门了
I opened it.

298
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:57,120
警官 算了
Sir? Okay.

299
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,126
太丢人了
So humiliating.

300
00:09:58,126 --> 00:10:00,257
饺子警官就那么把我扔在车后座
Officer Pierogi just banishes me to the backseat

301
00:10:00,257 --> 00:10:02,388
好像我只是搭车一样
like I'm just along for the ride.

302
00:10:02,388 --> 00:10:04,379
这本来就是"随警巡逻"
Well, it is called a "Ride-along". So...

303
00:10:04,379 --> 00:10:05,546
米奇尔
Mitchell!

304
00:10:05,546 --> 00:10:07,880
露西 小卡 这是露西
Oh, hey, Lucy, um -- Cam, this is Lucy.

305
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,800
今天就是她帮我们安排的
She's the one that set all this up for us.

306
00:10:09,800 --> 00:10:10,760
太谢谢你了
Thank you so much.

307
00:10:10,760 --> 00:10:12,660
-米奇尔今天特别开心 -那太好了
- Mitchell had a wonderful time. - Oh, great.

308
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:14,740
-意思是你同意了吗 -问题是什么
- So, does that mean the answer's "Yes"? - What's the question?

309
00:10:14,740 --> 00:10:15,720
几周来
Oh, I've been trying for weeks

310
00:10:15,720 --> 00:10:17,240
我都在试图说服他当检察官
to get this guy to become prosecutor.

311
00:10:18,056 --> 00:10:19,793
你是说《法律与秩序》中的
Y-- You mean, like, Angie Harmon on --

312
00:10:20,283 --> 00:10:20,636
安吉·哈蒙
on "Law and Order"

313
00:10:20,962 --> 00:10:21,893
或者《洛城法网》中的苏珊·黛
or Susan Dey on "L.A. Law"?

314
00:10:22,220 --> 00:10:24,060
或者做这份工作的男人
Or a man who does that job.

315
00:10:24,060 --> 00:10:27,060
那你怎么没和我说呢
Okay, well, why didn't you tell me about this?

316
00:10:27,060 --> 00:10:29,580
你们先好好讨论吧
I'm going to give you guys a minute.

317
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:31,750
但是米奇尔 周一之前你得告诉我结果
But, um, Mitchell, I really need to know by Monday.

318
00:10:31,750 --> 00:10:33,200
不然我就得去找别人了 好吗
Otherwise, I have to move on to someone else, okay?

319
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:34,244
-好 -很高兴见到你
- Okay. ?- It was nice to meet you.

320
00:10:34,244 --> 00:10:35,949
-我也是 -再见
- Nice to meet you. ?- Bye!

321
00:10:36,576 --> 00:10:37,478
很抱歉
Okay, I'm -- I'm sorry

322
00:10:37,478 --> 00:10:38,927
我没和你说这份工作的事
I -- I didn't tell you about the job.

323
00:10:38,927 --> 00:10:40,600
只是这是个重大改变
It's -- it's just a big change,

324
00:10:40,600 --> 00:10:42,320
我希望自己做出这个决定
and I wanted to make this decision on my own.

325
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,436
知道吗 这是好消息
You know what, here's the good news.

326
00:10:43,436 --> 00:10:45,260
-你有个很棒的工作机会 -嗯
- You have a fantastic job offer... ?- Mm-hmm.

327
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:46,940
如果今天我们学到了什么
...and if today taught us anything,

328
00:10:46,940 --> 00:10:48,840
那就是你对这世界有激情
it's that you have a passion for this world.

329
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:50,880
实际上 如果今天我们学到了什么
Well, actually, if today taught me anything,

330
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:52,232
那就是我绝对不想要这份工作
it's that I definitely do not want this job.

331
00:10:52,232 --> 00:10:54,056
我要去找露西
I'm -- I'm gonna go find Lucy.

332
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:59,740
真好 我迟到了
Oh, good. I'm late.

333
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:03,454
我在努力不受日程的控制
I'm trying to free myself of the calendar.

334
00:11:03,454 --> 00:11:05,640
我按生物周期节律生活
I live by my circadian rhythms.

335
00:11:05,640 --> 00:11:06,960
真重要
So important!

336
00:11:06,960 --> 00:11:11,260
妮可 这是我外公杰
Nicole, this is my grandfather, Jay.

337
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:11,980
你好吗
How do you do?

338
00:11:11,980 --> 00:11:15,120
这位是辣酱专家 我妻子歌洛莉亚
And this is the sauce maven herself, my wife, Gloria.

339
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,820
很高兴见到你
Very nice to meet you.

340
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:18,740
我喜欢你的口音
Oh, I love your accent.

341
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:20,598
我之前争取了
You know, I was up for the role

342
00:11:20,598 --> 00:11:22,200
墨西哥矮子毒枭情妇的位子
of El Chapo's mistress.

343
00:11:22,200 --> 00:11:25,140
我没看那部电影
Oh, I did not see that movie.

344
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:26,880
什么电影
What movie?

345
00:11:26,880 --> 00:11:30,600
我们很感激
And we appreciate you taking time

346
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:33,320
你在繁忙的工作中抽出时间
from your busy schedule here at NERP.

347
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,080
这是个很有活力的组织
It's a dynamite organization.

348
00:11:35,080 --> 00:11:37,240
我是铁杆粉 我喜欢你做的事
I'm a big fan. Love what you're doing.

349
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:38,640
你在干什么
What are you doing?

350
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:40,480
我在推销 我在这样做
I was selling. That's what I was doing.

351
00:11:40,600 --> 00:11:43,020
我不知道这邪教宣传的是什么理念
I don't know what nonsense this cult was pushing,

352
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:44,000
但反正最后
but at the end of the day,

353
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,500
他们会参与辣酱生意
they were gonna be in the sauce business.

354
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:47,420
这些辣椒
And so, these peppers

355
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:49,940
是歌洛莉亚辣酱的核心
are the heart of Gloria's sauce.

356
00:11:49,940 --> 00:11:53,100
但这是成品
But this is the finished product,

357
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,020
当然
of course --

358
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:58,080
莎莎辣酱
the Salsa Atomica.

359
00:12:03,620 --> 00:12:05,280
很有辣椒感
Mmm! Peppery!

360
00:12:05,280 --> 00:12:08,180
她有精细的味觉
She has a sophisticated palate!

361
00:12:09,660 --> 00:12:12,180
我能感觉到治愈效果
I can feel the healing.

362
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:13,820
也许那就是你容光焕发的原因
Maybe that's why you're glowing.

363
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,020
是我疯了 还是她真的容光焕发
Am I crazy or is she glowing?

364
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:17,520
绝对是容光焕发
Totally glowing!

365
00:12:17,520 --> 00:12:22,000
歌洛莉亚 我发现你有点安静
Gloria, I notice that you're really kind of quiet.

366
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,356
是缺乏维生素D吗
Is that a vitamin D thing?

367
00:12:23,356 --> 00:12:25,400
我们有袜子能解决这一问题
'Cause we have socks that can address that.

368
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:26,660
不 我只是...
No, I'm just --

369
00:12:26,660 --> 00:12:29,540
让我卖掉这个很难
you know, it's hard for me to sell this.

370
00:12:29,540 --> 00:12:31,970
这在我家族里传了五代
It's been in my family for five generations.

371
00:12:31,970 --> 00:12:33,500
他们大部分15岁就有了孩子
Most of them had kids at 15.

372
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:37,060
我村里一直很动荡
Things were not always easy in my village.

373
00:12:37,060 --> 00:12:39,080
但我们
But the one thing

374
00:12:39,080 --> 00:12:42,000
一直可以依靠的一样东西就是辣酱
that we could always count on was the sauce

375
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,300
这是由几种神奇的哥伦比亚辣椒混合而成
made from this blend of magical Colombian peppers.

376
00:12:45,941 --> 00:12:46,573
也许是因为
Well, maybe it was just the way

377
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:48,700
水从山上流下来
the water came down the mountain

378
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,960
在我们的家庭农场周围蜿蜒
and curved around our family farm.

379
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:53,507
我喜欢山和曲线
I love mountains and curves.

380
00:12:53,507 --> 00:12:54,700
太诺普了
So NERP!

381
00:12:54,700 --> 00:12:55,680
我记得
You know, I remember

382
00:12:55,680 --> 00:12:58,320
我祖母每周日为我做饭
my grandmother cooking for me every Sunday.

383
00:12:58,320 --> 00:13:00,140
我会抓着她的围裙
I would hold on to her apron

384
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:01,700
跟她在厨房里转来转去
and follow her around the kitchen

385
00:13:01,700 --> 00:13:03,200
而她在准备辣酱
while she prepared her sauce.

386
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,400
她会把勺子送到我嘴边
She would hold out the spoon to me

387
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:06,680
说 "尝尝
and say, "Taste this.

388
00:13:06,680 --> 00:13:08,320
这是你的家"
It's your familia."

389
00:13:08,368 --> 00:13:10,233
我觉得诺普公司是我家
I feel like NERP is my familia.

390
00:13:10,281 --> 00:13:11,644
是啊 我们圣诞节都在这里过的
Yeah, we were all here on Christmas.

391
00:13:12,280 --> 00:13:15,132
也许现在是时候了
Maybe it is the right time.

392
00:13:15,132 --> 00:13:17,000
我祖母不在了
My abuela is gone.

393
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,060
叔祖母都不在了
My great aunts are all gone.

394
00:13:20,060 --> 00:13:22,710
河道被改直了
They straightened the river.

395
00:13:22,710 --> 00:13:24,860
诺普公司可以重新把它变弯
NERP can re-curve it.

396
00:13:24,860 --> 00:13:26,560
也许是时候跟
Maybe it is the time to say "Goodbye"

397
00:13:26,560 --> 00:13:29,120
唯一一样有真正联系的东西说"再见"了...
to the one thing that is a real connection to --

398
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:30,820
你不会跟任何东西说再见
You're not saying "Goodbye" To anything.

399
00:13:30,820 --> 00:13:32,760
交易结束了
This deal is done!

400
00:13:32,760 --> 00:13:36,280
很抱歉这样为难你
I'm so sorry to have put you in this position.

401
00:13:36,280 --> 00:13:38,317
我绝对不会让你背弃...
I will never ask you to turn your back --

402
00:13:38,317 --> 00:13:40,820
-你搞砸了 蠢蛋 -什么
- You blew it, you dummy! - What?

403
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:42,940
我本来想卖掉那白痴辣酱的
I wanted to sell that stupid sauce!

404
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:47,340
等等 我搞不懂了
Wait a minute. I'm confused.

405
00:13:47,340 --> 00:13:49,260
你为什么要告诉她交易取消了
Why did you tell her that the deal was off?

406
00:13:49,260 --> 00:13:50,794
我是想保护你的家族传承
I was trying to protect your legacy.

407
00:13:50,794 --> 00:13:52,102
什么传承 根本没有传承
What legacy? There's not legacy.

408
00:13:52,102 --> 00:13:55,304
整个故事都是我瞎编来抬高价格的
I invented that whole story to drive up the price.

409
00:13:55,304 --> 00:13:56,621
你确定你是销售业的吗
Are you sure you're in sales?

410
00:13:56,621 --> 00:13:57,460
那照片呢
What about the pictures?

411
00:13:57,460 --> 00:13:58,561
是我从曼尼的
I cut them out

412
00:13:58,561 --> 00:14:01,960
《国家地理》旧杂志上剪下来的
from Manny's National Geographic old magazines.

413
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,380
瞧瞧 这里甚至还有
Look, there's even a picture

414
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:06,460
环球影城游玩的照片
at the Universal Studios tour.

415
00:14:06,460 --> 00:14:08,789
背景是《惊魂记》的房子
That's the "Psycho" House in the back!

416
00:14:08,789 --> 00:14:10,520
所以你想摆脱辣酱生意吗
So, you want to get rid of the business?

417
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,840
是啊 我讨厌它
Yes, I hate that sauce.

418
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:13,940
像狗一样烦
It's a dog!

419
00:14:13,940 --> 00:14:16,320
我在市里有好多储存室
I have storage lockers all over town

420
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,340
里面都是辣酱罐
full of jars.

421
00:14:17,340 --> 00:14:21,045
我试过冲进马桶 但它腐蚀了管道
I tried to flush it, but it eats up the pipes.

422
00:14:21,045 --> 00:14:22,209
你可以直接告诉我啊
You could've just told me.

423
00:14:22,209 --> 00:14:24,794
我不想承认你是对的
I didn't want to admit that you were right

424
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,580
我这辈子都得听你说
and have to hear "I told you so"

425
00:14:26,580 --> 00:14:27,980
"我跟你说过了吧"
for the rest of my life.

426
00:14:27,980 --> 00:14:31,000
是你这辈子
Well, your life.

427
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,240
但这是我结婚后自己做的
But, it was the first thing I was doing on my own

428
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,580
第一个事业
after getting married.

429
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:35,960
结果很失败
And it was a failure.

430
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:38,720
亲爱的 你别把自己逼太紧
Honey, you've got to cut yourself some slack.

431
00:14:38,720 --> 00:14:40,900
你知道我抛弃过多少
Do you know how many ideas I had to dump

432
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:41,860
行不通的点子吗
because they weren't working?

433
00:14:42,328 --> 00:14:45,132
我曾是职业回力球联赛的隐名合伙人
I was a silent partner of a professional Jai Alai league.

434
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,220
是用汤勺玩球的那项运动吗
With the ball and the scoopy thing?

435
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:48,460
你俩 搞什么呢
You guys! What was that?!

436
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:50,174
现在我再也没法得到我自己的豆袋椅了
Now I'm never gonna get my own bean bag chair.

437
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:52,140
不 现在没事了 我们想卖了
No, it's gonna be fine. We want to sell now.

438
00:14:52,140 --> 00:14:53,920
太迟了 她翻篇了
It's too late. She's moved on.

439
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:55,440
妮可不给第二次机会
Nicole doesn't give second chances.

440
00:14:55,440 --> 00:14:56,763
主要是因为《第二次机会》是
Mostly because that's the name

441
00:14:56,763 --> 00:14:58,680
她和安德鲁·麦卡锡失败的浪漫喜剧的名字
of a failed rom-com she made with Andrew McCarthy.

442
00:14:58,680 --> 00:15:00,900
我之前就是在那部剧上看到的她
That's where I've seen her before!

443
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:02,400
听着 这还没结束
Listen, this isn't over.

444
00:15:02,400 --> 00:15:04,960
我之前有过背水一战的时候
I've had my back against the wall before.

445
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,180
丹佛 橱柜展览会 97年
Denver, Closet-Con, '97.

446
00:15:07,180 --> 00:15:09,655
我仓库里都是雪松货架
I had a warehouse full of cedar shelves.

447
00:15:09,655 --> 00:15:11,239
落基山脉刮来一场风暴
A storm blew in over the Rockies --

448
00:15:11,239 --> 00:15:12,632
你卖了橱柜 我知道
You sold the closet. I get it.

449
00:15:12,632 --> 00:15:15,723
-我们上去吧 -故事情节还有很多的
- Let's go up there. - There's a whole story here.

450
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:18,400
妮可 瞧瞧谁回来了
Nicole! Look who came back!

451
00:15:18,400 --> 00:15:20,000
我们刚在外面交谈
Listen, we were just talking outside,

452
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,580
也许我有点轻率了
and maybe I was a little rash.

453
00:15:21,580 --> 00:15:22,700
真的吗
Really?

454
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:24,920
也许太轻率[皮疹]了
Maybe a big rash.

455
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:26,630
很高兴听你这样说
I'm so happy to hear you say that

456
00:15:26,630 --> 00:15:27,860
你们走后我一直
'cause I haven't been able to stop

457
00:15:27,860 --> 00:15:29,393
忍不住吃你们的辣酱
eating your salsa since you left.

458
00:15:29,393 --> 00:15:30,840
你没有办法证明是吃了我们辣酱
There's no way to prove that.

459
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:33,020
顺便问问
Apropos of nothing,

460
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:36,420
你信西药吗
do you believe in Western medicine?

461
00:15:40,133 --> 00:15:41,301
爽
Ahh! Sweet.

462
00:15:42,153 --> 00:15:43,001
卢克
Luke!

463
00:15:43,380 --> 00:15:44,040
爸爸
Dad?

464
00:15:44,051 --> 00:15:45,629
很需要你 伙计
Need you bad, buddy.

465
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:48,040
-你为什么在叫 -别告诉你妈妈
- Why are you yelling? - Oh, don't tell Mom,

466
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,340
我运动过猛 我耳朵都堵了
but I worked out too hard, and it clogged my ears.

467
00:15:50,340 --> 00:15:52,460
我需要一些冰块 还有热敷袋
I need some ice. And a heating pad.

468
00:15:52,460 --> 00:15:53,276
还有止痛药
And some aspirin.

469
00:15:53,276 --> 00:15:55,520
还有不需要嚼的食物 比如果冻或汤
And some soft foods, like Jell-o or soup.

470
00:15:55,520 --> 00:15:57,980
你能做水煮蛋吗 能听到我说话吗
Can you poach an egg? Can you even hear me?!

471
00:15:57,980 --> 00:16:00,160
您好
Hi.

472
00:16:00,160 --> 00:16:01,760
好的
Okay.

473
00:16:01,760 --> 00:16:04,440
-我马上回来 -好吧
- I'll be right back. -Okay...

474
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:05,777
怎么了
What's going on?

475
00:16:05,777 --> 00:16:09,500
别告诉你爸 但我动不了了
Don't tell you father, but I can't move.

476
00:16:09,500 --> 00:16:11,260
帮我把浴缸放好水 等放好了
Start me a tub and when it's ready,

477
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:12,840
把我抱到楼上再放进浴缸里
carry me upstairs and put me in it.

478
00:16:12,840 --> 00:16:14,200
你能帮我烧壶水泡茶吗
Can you boil water for tea?

479
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:15,161
可以吧
I guess.

480
00:16:15,161 --> 00:16:16,788
卢克 你上哪去啦 哥们
Luke, what happened, chief?

481
00:16:16,788 --> 00:16:18,664
我在帮妈弄点东西
Uh, I'm helping Mom with something!

482
00:16:18,664 --> 00:16:19,940
别暴露啊
Don't say that!

483
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:21,660
克莱尔 没事吧
Claire, everything okay?!

484
00:16:21,660 --> 00:16:24,180
没事啊 我就拉伸一下
Yes! I'm just stretching!

485
00:16:24,180 --> 00:16:26,500
我也是
Me, too!

486
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:27,579
卢克
Luke!

487
00:16:27,579 --> 00:16:30,440
他来帮忙我弄一些电脑的东西
Uh, he's helping me with something on the computer!

488
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:32,189
他可会弄电脑了
He's so good at computers!

489
00:16:32,189 --> 00:16:34,140
太聪明了 这孩子
Oh, such a smart boy!

490
00:16:34,140 --> 00:16:36,320
好了 够了 你们俩简直神经病
Okay, all right. This is nuts.

491
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,140
什么 别
What? No.

492
00:16:37,140 --> 00:16:38,800
哎哟喂
Oh, boy.

493
00:16:42,900 --> 00:16:43,340
你好啊
Hi.

494
00:16:43,434 --> 00:16:45,426
-你好啊 亲爱的 -宝贝
- Oh, hi, honey. - Hey, sweetie.

495
00:16:45,521 --> 00:16:45,985
你还好吗
Are you good?

496
00:16:46,079 --> 00:16:47,885
还不错啊
Oh, yeah, yeah.

497
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:49,880
-那你呢 -棒呆了
- Are you good? - ?So good!

498
00:16:49,880 --> 00:16:51,200
我不知道你们俩是在搞什么鬼
I don't know what's going on here,

499
00:16:51,200 --> 00:16:52,700
但你们俩都不好
but neither of you are good!

500
00:16:52,700 --> 00:16:54,360
如果你们想要有人照顾你们
If you want someone to take care of you,

501
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:58,840
我建议等你们俩能动了 再生个孩子吧
I suggest once you can move, you make another baby.

502
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:01,580
你也浑身疼吗
You're hurting, too?

503
00:17:01,580 --> 00:17:03,340
那场比赛可真是要亲命了
That race, it almost destroyed me.

504
00:17:03,340 --> 00:17:05,600
我可能这辈子只能维持这个姿势了
And I have to spend the rest of my life in this position.

505
00:17:05,742 --> 00:17:06,468
我们这是在干嘛啊
What are we doing?

506
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:09,418
我们这比赛的状态就像两个不中用的中年人
We're competing like a couple of 40-year-olds.

507
00:17:09,560 --> 00:17:10,940
我好几个月没健身了
I haven't worked out in months.

508
00:17:10,940 --> 00:17:12,060
但你这是怎么回事
But, what's up with you?

509
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:14,020
你不是整天往篮球场跑吗
You're out on that basketball court all the time.

510
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:16,900
克莱尔
Claire.

511
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:20,440
我想介绍你认识一个人
There's someone I'd like for you to meet...

512
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:25,620
这是牛逼负鼠哥
This is Awesome Possum.

513
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:27,000
我不是去运动
Instead of working out,

514
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,720
我都是跟超酷的朋友们玩机器人大战
my super cool friends and I have epic robot battles.

515
00:17:29,720 --> 00:17:31,560
我唯一会流汗的时候
The only time I break a sweat

516
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:33,440
是我们跑去买冰淇淋的时候
is when we run after the ice cream truck.

517
00:17:33,571 --> 00:17:34,909
半途而废的感觉就是这样吗
Is this what giving up feels like?

518
00:17:35,040 --> 00:17:36,980
不算 我们一起放弃就不算啊
No, not if we do it together.

519
00:17:36,980 --> 00:17:41,340
我们一起用合理的速度
Let's boldly walk forward at a reasonable pace

520
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:42,420
大步迈进
into this new future

521
00:17:42,420 --> 00:17:44,780
这个不用假装我们还宝刀未老的未来
where we don't have to pretend to be strong or fast.

522
00:17:44,780 --> 00:17:46,640
-我能坦白一件事吗 -可以啊
- Can I make a confession? - Yeah.

523
00:17:46,640 --> 00:17:48,740
有时候我会下午五点就饿了
Sometimes, I get hungry at, like, 5:00.

524
00:17:48,740 --> 00:17:49,920
我也是啊
Me, too!

525
00:17:49,920 --> 00:17:51,600
我们开始提早吃晚饭吧
Let's start having early dinners!

526
00:17:51,600 --> 00:17:52,793
那时间太合理了
It makes so much sense.

527
00:17:52,793 --> 00:17:55,344
老人家太聪明了
Old people are wise.

528
00:17:56,112 --> 00:17:58,860
不行 负鼠哥 不行
Oh, no, Poss! No!

529
00:17:58,860 --> 00:18:00,210
不行 我给了你生命
No! I gave you life!

530
00:18:00,210 --> 00:18:02,040
佩里博士 我是卢克·邓菲
Dr. Perry, this is Luke Dunphy.

531
00:18:02,040 --> 00:18:03,380
忘了我之前说的话吧
Forget what I said.

532
00:18:03,380 --> 00:18:05,123
我想要今天就开始上大学
I'd like to start college today.

533
00:18:05,123 --> 00:18:07,133
别啊 卢克
No! Luke!

534
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:12,220
米奇尔 进来
Mitchell, come in here.

535
00:18:12,958 --> 00:18:15,552
小房间 大镜子 手铐
Wow. Small room, big mirror, handcuffs.

536
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:16,484
饮品超贵
Overcharge for drinks,

537
00:18:16,484 --> 00:18:17,760
这里很可能是西好莱坞的情趣酒吧呢
and this could be a bar in West Hollywood.

538
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,040
跟我说 你为什么不接这份工作
Okay, why aren't you taking this job?

539
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:20,840
-我不想啊 -为什么
- I don't want to. - ?Why not?

540
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:22,503
你不喜欢自由职业 你几乎都没在做
You hate freelancing. You're barely doing it.

541
00:18:22,503 --> 00:18:23,940
我还挺忙的呢
I-I'm plenty busy.

542
00:18:23,940 --> 00:18:25,540
是吗 因为其实呢
Are you? Because you know what?

543
00:18:25,540 --> 00:18:27,200
我跟莉莉看到你
Lily and I saw you

544
00:18:27,200 --> 00:18:29,200
往口袋里放面包屑
putting breadcrumbs in your pocket the other day.

545
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:31,280
你是不是又开始下午没事干
Are you back to spending your afternoons

546
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:32,760
就跑去公园喂鸽子了 米奇尔
with the pigeons in the park, Mitchell?

547
00:18:32,821 --> 00:18:34,078
什么 它们饿嘛
W-- You know, they're hungry.

548
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:35,800
不 是你饥肠辘辘
No, you're hungry.

549
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:37,320
急需人生目标补充
For a purpose.

550
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:40,040
就觉得不适合我嘛
It's just not my thing.

551
00:18:40,040 --> 00:18:42,420
坐下
Sit down. ?

552
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,960
不适合你是吗
Not your thing, huh?

553
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:46,640
看好了 这是我今天下午抓拍的你
Okay, well, I snapped this picture of you this afternoon.

554
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:48,340
你认出了这张照片里的人吗
Do you recognize the person in this picture?

555
00:18:48,912 --> 00:18:50,427
认出来了 是我 你刚说过啊
Uh, Yes, it's me. You just said that, so...

556
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:52,640
好的 那你看看你脸上是什么表情
Okay, well, what is the expression on your face?

557
00:18:52,640 --> 00:18:54,900
-你在干嘛 -我问了你问题
- What are you doing? - I asked a question!

558
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:57,920
"你脸上是什么表情"
"What is the expression on your face?"

559
00:18:57,920 --> 00:18:58,700
是在笑
It's a smile.

560
00:18:58,789 --> 00:19:00,972
那你会怎么描述这个"笑"
And how would you describe this..."smile"?

561
00:19:01,061 --> 00:19:02,315
是开怀大笑
Well, from ear-to-ear.

562
00:19:02,405 --> 00:19:03,719
勃利斯基上哪去买我的甜甜圈了
Wh-where's Blitz with my donut?

563
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:04,831
想吃甜甜圈
You'll get a donut

564
00:19:04,920 --> 00:19:07,760
等我听到我要的答案了你就能吃 你个垃圾
when I get answers, you piece of trash!

565
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:13,400
我的老天啊 这...
Oh, my gosh, what --

566
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:15,540
这到底是怎么回事呢
what's happening here, huh?

567
00:19:15,540 --> 00:19:17,080
抱歉 米奇尔 其实呢
I'm sorry, Mitchell. You know what?

568
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:18,440
我只是来帮你的
I'm just here to help you.

569
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,680
这里就是我们俩谈谈心
Let's just you and me talk.

570
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:21,840
你是认真的吗 一人分饰好警察坏警察
Are you seriously trying to good cop/bad cop me?

571
00:19:21,840 --> 00:19:24,220
不是 我只是想要了解了解你
No, I'm trying to get some understanding

572
00:19:24,220 --> 00:19:27,300
因为今天一整个下午我都跟你在一起
because I was with you the entire afternoon

573
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:30,820
而你无法否认你今天玩得很开心吧
and you can't deny you had a great time.

574
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,020
等等 除了...
Wait a minute -- except for when --

575
00:19:32,020 --> 00:19:33,820
除了你下车去追那个人那会儿
when you got out of the car to chase that guy down.

576
00:19:33,820 --> 00:19:34,700
米奇尔 那段时间发生了什么
Mitchell, what happened?

577
00:19:34,700 --> 00:19:35,360
没有啊
Nothing.

578
00:19:35,360 --> 00:19:41,480
我们去追那个不负责任的爸爸时
Okay, we were chasing after that deadbeat guy,

579
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:43,340
然后我开始 开始想到他的孩子
and I started -- I started thinking about his kid.

580
00:19:43,340 --> 00:19:46,200
我当时就想着抓住他 让他付出代价
And I just -- I wanted to catch him and make him pay.

581
00:19:46,322 --> 00:19:48,361
然后斯塔勃利斯基把他按倒在地
And then, Stablitzky got him on the ground

582
00:19:48,483 --> 00:19:51,678
我看到他的表情 他...
and I saw his face and he was --

583
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,500
他当时在害怕
he was scared.

584
00:19:52,500 --> 00:19:53,860
他也是个活生生的人
There's a person there.

585
00:19:53,860 --> 00:19:55,340
我并不知道事情的全部真相
I don't know the whole story.

586
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:58,480
我觉得我没办法轻易就把人丢进大牢
I don't think that I can just toss someone into prison.

587
00:19:58,480 --> 00:20:01,140
-米奇尔 别... -你看 所以我不想跟你说
- Mitchell, come... - See? This is why I didn't tell you, okay?

588
00:20:01,140 --> 00:20:02,260
你会批判我
You're judging me.

589
00:20:02,260 --> 00:20:04,000
你就是那种严厉 正义型的人
You're the tough, justice guy,

590
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:05,691
但我... 我很心软
and I'm just -- I'm soft.

591
00:20:05,691 --> 00:20:07,480
不 你很公正
No, you're fair.

592
00:20:07,480 --> 00:20:09,880
当然啦 你可能很贴心很敏感
And, of course, you can be thoughtful and sensitive.

593
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:11,480
但你也可以很严厉啊
But you can be tough.

594
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:14,400
你还记得我们看《狮子王》时 我们前面
You remember the woman in front of us at "Lion King"

595
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:16,800
一直把包装纸弄出声音的大帽子女人吗
with the candy wrappers and the big, giant hat?

596
00:20:16,800 --> 00:20:18,720
-我对她大爆发啊 -是啊
- Whoo, I went crazy on her. - You sure did.

597
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,040
就是那份激情
And it is that passion

598
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:23,640
能让你成为一个很棒的检察官
that would make you an amazing prosecutor.

599
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:25,580
-你真这么觉得吗 -当然啦
- Do you really think so? - Of course.

600
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:28,120
而且世界上也没有
And nothing would thrill me more

601
00:20:28,120 --> 00:20:29,500
比起你迈向人生新篇章
than to watch you embark

602
00:20:29,500 --> 00:20:31,500
更让我激动不已的事情了
on this new chapter of your life.

603
00:20:31,500 --> 00:20:35,100
但... 但薪水会少非常多
It is -- it is a lot less money, though.

604
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:39,220
我们也不着急今天就得做决定嘛
Well, you know, we don't have to decide today.

605
00:20:43,165 --> 00:20:44,440
两位
Guys.

606
00:20:44,440 --> 00:20:47,148
两位 你们又把我落下了
Guys! You forgot me again.

607
00:20:47,148 --> 00:20:49,780
我也想吃炸玉米饼
I'd like tacos too.

608
00:20:49,780 --> 00:20:50,880
米奇尔
Mitchell.

609
00:20:52,255 --> 00:20:53,237
米奇尔
Mitchell!

610
00:20:54,504 --> 00:20:55,480
海莉
Haley.

611
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:57,260
请进来我办公室一下
In my office please.

612
00:20:57,260 --> 00:20:57,687
来了
Coming.

613
00:20:57,687 --> 00:20:58,520
好吧
Okay.

614
00:20:58,520 --> 00:21:04,560
你在哪里呢
Where are you.

615
00:21:04,560 --> 00:21:06,800
我的脸出事了
Something happened to my face.

616
00:21:08,707 --> 00:21:09,987
我去
I got...

617
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:13,960
我去吧
I got it.

618
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:17,180
它去
He's got it.
